<title>INDIA: INDIA SAYS PRIVATISATION GOING ON SMOOTHLY.</title>
<headline>INDIA SAYS PRIVATISATION GOING ON SMOOTHLY.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Finance Minister P. Chidambaram said on Friday the government's sale of stakes in state-owned companies was proceeding smoothly.</p>
<p>&quot;The government will be able to realise its target of raising 48 billion rupees though disinvestment of shares in public sector undertakings (PSUs) this year,&quot; Chidambaram said in reply to a lawmaker's question in the lower house of parliament, Lok Sabha.</p>
<p>He was referring to the target for 1997/98 (April-March).</p>
<p>&quot;The disinvestment process is going on smoothly. No attempt is being made to deliberately slow it down,&quot; Chidambaram said, referring to criticism that there was a slowdown in the partial privatisation process.</p>
<p>The government decided last month to sell stakes in Container Corporation of India (Concor), Mahanagar Telephone Nigam Ltd, Indian Oil Corp and the Gas Authority of India Ltd.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi Newsroom (91) 11-301-2024; Fax (91) 11-301-4043</p>
